{"type":"message","id":"3691d0b3","parentId":"f1ec40ca","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:05:26.540Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Tue 2026-02-17 22:35 GMT+5:30] Create a comprehensive plan for assigning dedicated models to each agent (coder, social, osint, generalist) instead of using the global default.\n\nContext:\n- Current setup: All agents use the default model `openrouter/stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free`\n- Goal: Tailor models per agent based on their specialization, cost, and capability needs\n- This requires careful configuration planning and potentially different providers\n\nPlease produce a structured plan covering:\n\n1. **Assessment** — what each agent does and what model capabilities they need\n   - Coder: code generation, debugging, possibly needs large context, reasoning\n   - Social Media: content creation, tone adaptation, maybe image understanding\n   - OSINT Analyst: research, fact-checking, web search integration, summarization\n   - Generalist: versatile tasks, maybe cost-effective model\n\n2. **Model Recommendations** — specific provider/model choices for each agent, with reasoning:\n   - Consider: cost (free vs paid), context window, reasoning ability, speed, multimodal needs\n   - Options: OpenRouter free models, Anthropic Claude, OpenAI GPT, local models if needed\n   - Justify each choice with trade-offs\n\n3. **Configuration Changes** — exactly what to update in `openclaw.json`:\n   - How to set per-agent `model.primary` overrides\n   - Any necessary `models` catalog additions\n   - Provider authentication requirements\n   - Example JSON patches\n\n4. **Migration Steps** — how to roll out safely:\n   - Phase 1: configure models without switching (prepare)\n   - Phase 2: switch one agent as test (e.g., Generalist)\n   - Phase 3: monitor costs and performance\n   - Phase 4: switch remaining agents\n   - Rollback plan if something breaks\n\n5. **Cost Tracking** — how to monitor spend per agent after divergence\n\n6. **Risks & Mitigations** — e.g., provider outages, API key rotation, quota exhaustion\n\nDeliverable: A clear, actionable plan with timelines and specific config snippets.\n\nReturn the full plan in a structured format (markdown with sections)."}],"timestamp":1771347926535}}
